    {
      "id": "triads-applied",
      "title": "Triads — Applied",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** theory | **Tier:** applied | **Difficulty:** 4/10\n**Prerequisites:** Triads — Introduction\n**Tags:** triads, inversions, voice-leading"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Triad **inversions** change bass note while keeping the same pitch classes. Voice-leading connects chords smoothly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "inversions",
      "title": "Inversions",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "- **Root position**: root in bass (C-E-G)\n- **First inversion**: third in bass (E-G-C)\n- **Second inversion**: fifth in bass (G-C-E)\n\nFigured bass: 5/3, 6, 6/4 — advanced tier in figured-bass lesson."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "voice-leading-basics",
      "title": "Voice-leading basics",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Move voices by step when possible. Avoid parallel perfect fifths and octaves in strict counterpoint; in folk accompaniment, practicality often wins."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
