  "reading_list": [],
  "quiz_markdown": "### Q1. First inversion has the third in the bass.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q2. Second inversion has the fifth in the bass.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q3. Root position is most stable.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q4. Inversions change harmonic function labels in strict theory.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q5. Voice-leading prefers stepwise motion.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q6. I–V–I uses root-position triads commonly.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q7. First inversion smooths bass lines.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q8. Applied triads support session backup.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q9. Doubling the third in first inversion is common.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q10. Cadences use specific inversion patterns.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q11. Parallel fifths are avoided in strict voice-leading.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q12. Triad inversions share the same three notes.\n\n**Answer:** True",
